      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "High. Quantized conductance in ballistic quantum point contacts provided a direct, experimentally accessible signature of quantum transport and helped establish mesoscopic physics.",
        "attribution": "The proposed names are associated with the early experimental demonstrations. The original papers and chronology should determine how credit is apportioned between the groups.",
        "maturity": "The effect is robust and foundational, confirmed across systems and central to later work on nanoscale transport.",
