      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "High. The discovery of conducting, strongly correlated electronic states at oxide interfaces revealed phenomena absent from the constituent bulk materials and opened a broad field of interface quantum matter.",
        "attribution": "The proposed names are tied to foundational interface growth and characterization. Experimental records are especially important for assigning original contributions to the interface and its properties.",
        "maturity": "The initial result has been extensively investigated, with many related interface phenomena established, though their mechanisms and material dependence remain active topics.",
